+Steady-state events per consumed PV tile on the kept direct route:
+
+- P payload generation/storage:
+  - Producer waits `p_stage_reusable[buf]` only when the two-slot P ring reuses a previously-seen slot.
+  - Score-derived E2M1 payload is stored directly into `p_fp4_stage[buf]`.
+  - One proxy publish/fence: `fp4pv_publish_shared_backing_proxy_only()`.
+  - Consumer does not wait a separate payload semaphore; payload visibility is included in the direct P-scale proof.
+  - PV consumer arrives `p_stage_reusable[p_buf]` once after PV issue.
+- P-scale TMEM:
+  - No separate producer wait on `p_sc_tmem_reusable` because reuse is folded with P-stage reuse.
+  - Producer issues one x1 P-scale TMEM store for `p_score_mx_packed_scales`.
+  - Producer executes one `fp4pv_tmem_store_wait()`.
+  - Producer arrives `p_sc_tmem_ready[p_sc_slot]` once.
+  - PV consumer waits `p_sc_tmem_ready[p_sc_slot]` once.
+  - No `p_quant_ready` wait/arrive and no `p_sc_tmem_reusable` arrive for this route.
+- V-scale TMEM:
+  - Producer V-scale warp waits `v_sc_tmem_reusable[v_buf]` once per slot reuse after the two-slot V ring is full.
+  - Producer waits `v_arrived[v_buf]`, stages V scale to TMEM with `fp4pv_load_mxnv_scale_async_cluster`, and arrives `v_sc_tmem_ready[v_buf]` once.
+  - PV consumer waits `v_sc_tmem_ready[v_buf]` once.
+  - PV consumer arrives `v_sc_tmem_reusable[v_buf]` once after PV issue.
+- PV issue ordering:
+  - Before MMA: `tensor_load_wait()` and `tensor_before_thread_sync()`.
+  - PV MMA issue through `issue_pv_stage`.
+  - Commit: `tensor_commit(pv_tmem_ready[0])`.
+
+Steady-state semaphore/proof count excluding tensor commit/load waits:
+
+- Producer-side P proof: 1 arrive (`p_sc_tmem_ready`), 1 proxy fence, 1 TMEM store wait, plus 1 P-stage reuse wait when the two-slot ring wraps.
+- Consumer-side P proof/reuse: 1 wait (`p_sc_tmem_ready`), 1 arrive (`p_stage_reusable`).
+- Producer-side V proof/reuse: 1 V-scale reusable wait after the two-slot ring fills, 1 `v_arrived` wait, 1 arrive (`v_sc_tmem_ready`).
+- Consumer-side V proof/reuse: 1 wait (`v_sc_tmem_ready`), 1 arrive (`v_sc_tmem_reusable`).
+- There is already only one consumed-tile P proof on the direct route. P payload and P-scale are not split into separate consumer waits.
+
+Rejected split-K64 comparison:
+
+- Split-K64 preserved the x1 score-derived P-scale store, `fp4pv_tmem_store_wait`, proxy ordering, V-scale ping-pong, and kept qkscfix math.
+- It changed the P proof from one combined `p_sc_tmem_ready` consumer wait to one scale wait plus two half-payload waits (`p_online_k64_ready[buf][0]` and `[1]`).
+- It added two half-payload arrives and two half-payload waits per consumed tile compared with the kept direct path.
+- Measured result was correct but slower: H16/S2048 `+1.1607%`, H16/S4096 `+2.7327%`.
+- Conclusion: the current remaining bubble is not solved by starting PV earlier if doing so adds per-half payload protocol. The added waits/arrives dominate the intended overlap.
+
+Feed-ready audit decision:
+
+- A new coarse `pv_feed_ready[slot]` could only replace the current two consumer waits (`v_sc_tmem_ready` and `p_sc_tmem_ready`) if some producer-side owner proves both readiness conditions.
+- With current 3WG ownership, P readiness is produced by the quant/score-derived P path and V-scale readiness is produced by the producer V-scale warp. Combining them without a relay/feeder WG requires either:
+  - P/quant waits on `v_sc_tmem_ready`, then arrives `pv_feed_ready`; or
+  - V-scale producer waits on `p_sc_tmem_ready`, then arrives `pv_feed_ready`.
+- In both cases the total event count is not reduced: one consumer wait is moved to a producer-side wait and a new feed-ready arrive/wait is introduced. It also serializes one independent readiness stream behind the other and risks delaying V-scale ping-pong.
+- Keeping `p_sc_tmem_ready`/`v_sc_tmem_ready` plus adding `pv_feed_ready` would be strictly worse.
+- Therefore no source patch was made for a coarse feed-ready proof in this loop.
