+Score/output lifetime audit:
+
+- QK producer writes score slot `idx % SCORE_TMEM_SLOTS` and commits `scores_arrived[score_slot]`.
+- Quant waits `scores_arrived[score_slot]`, loads score TMEM into registers, then arrives `p_copy_done[copy_done_slot]`.
+- QK cannot safely reuse a score slot until `wait_score_copy_done(score_slot)` has observed that quant copied that slot.
+- The kept route also uses score slots as dual-output spare accumulators:
+  - `output_spare_tensor_for_score_idx(idx)` returns `d_tt_outputs(tt_score_base.addr + score_slot * C::Nb)` when `STATIC_ONLINE_MXFP4_DUAL_OUTPUT_ACCUM_SCORE_TMEM` is true.
+  - Direct-after-rescale is guarded by a static assert requiring score-TMEM accumulators and forbidding forced separate spare output.
+  - Output WG releases score-slot spare use through `dual_output_spare_reusable[score_slot]` only after merge/rescale ownership is complete.
+- Therefore each 128-column score slot has two live roles: the next QK score tile until `p_copy_done`, and the alternate output accumulator when a non-first PV tile cannot accumulate directly into main output.
+- Shrinking score width from 256 to 240 is not a local layout change. `d_tt_scores` is `tt<float, C::Mb, C::Nb>` and score slots are addressed as `tt_score_base.addr + score_slot * C::Nb`; the MMA score tile itself is 128 columns wide.
+- Replacing dual score with single score would free columns but would serialize or rewrite the kept decoupled QK/PV path and remove the output-spare alias that direct-after-rescale depends on. That is a new structural algorithm, not a safe footprint proof for this route.
+- Moving the spare output out of score TMEM would allocate another `C::Dvo = 128` output columns, making the TMEM budget worse, not better.
+- Main output at columns 256..383 is a full `Dvo=128` accumulator. There is no safe 16-column reduction without changing the output MMA accumulator shape.
