+Interpretation:
+
+- Even when `C::CLUSTER_SIZE > 1`, Q, Q-scale, K, and K-scale TMA calls use `cluster_mask = (1 << cta_rank)`, not a broadcast mask like `0b11`.
+- This is cluster TMA with a single-CTA destination mask, not real multicast.
+- Under the current cluster2 semantics, the one-bit masks are not just an oversight:
+  - Q is rank-specific because `q_tile_idx = t_coord.y + cta_rank`.
+  - K is rank-specific because `k_tile_idx = global_idx * C::CLUSTER_SIZE + cta_rank`.
+  - Q scale follows the Q tile.
+  - K scale follows the K tile.
+- Changing these masks to `0b11` in place would broadcast rank-specific data to both CTAs. That would either duplicate the wrong Q/K tile or have two ranks racing to overwrite the same destination slots with different coordinates.
