+Legality classification:
+
+- V payload multicast is not a legal mask-only probe for the current route. Current cluster2 V semantics split the Dvo rows by CTA rank; broadcasting one V tile to both ranks would duplicate rank0's rows into rank1's destination/semantic slot. Making V multicast useful would require a new macro-tile ownership where both CTAs consume the same V tile for different Q rows, plus matching PV/output ownership and shared layout changes.
+- K payload and K-scale multicast are plausible only in a new row-parallel cluster2 design where both CTAs use the same K tile for different Q rows. Current cluster2 code intentionally assigns different K tiles per rank, so changing `cluster_mask` to both CTAs would make rank1 compute with the wrong K tile and would alter online softmax/P/LSE ordering.
