+### 2026-06-14 Dvo/2 output ownership design audit
+
+User directive:
+
+- After rejecting full-V-per-rank, try the Dvo/2 output ownership + stitch/merge design if bounded.
+- Keep default VTMA/VSTMA qkscfix and manual-V qkscfix fallback untouched.
+- Build and correctness-gate S128/S2048 before timing.
+
+Source facts:
+
+- The dormant rowpar2 rank-local support currently maps CTA rank to row ownership: `q_tile_idx = t_coord.y + cta_rank`, `online_iters_for_row_cluster` advances by `cta_rank + 1`, and output store writes full `Dvo=128` to `t_coord.y + cta_rank`.
+- A Dvo/2 route cannot reuse that row-parallel ownership directly: rank 0 would write row tile `m` columns 0..63 and rank 1 would write row tile `m+1` columns 64..127, leaving each row half-missing.
+- A coherent Dvo/2 route must therefore be column-parallel, not row-parallel:
+  - both CTA ranks load/generate the same Q/K/P and same online softmax stats for row tile `m`;
+  - rank 0 loads V rows 0..63 and writes output columns 0..63;
+  - rank 1 loads V rows 64..127 and writes output columns 64..127;
+  - only one rank stores LSE to avoid duplicate global writes.
+- Existing manual V payload loader already uses `row_base = cta_rank * (Dvo / cluster_size)`, which is exactly the half-Dvo V ownership needed for a column-parallel prototype.
+- Existing prepared V-scale loader is not rank-offset for `Dvo=128`; this matches the current half-V cluster2 scale contract and can be staged rank-locally through the existing route-aware scale helper.
+- The output path is the main contract change:
+  - `d_tt_outputs` is currently `tt<float, Mb, Dvo>` and final normalization loops over `C::Dvo`;
+  - `G::o_tile` is a full `st_bf<Mb,Dvo>` and output writeback uses full-tile TMA store;
+  - a half-output route needs `tt<float, Mb, Dvo/2>` and a manual 64-column global store, or a new half-output TMA descriptor/globals type.
+
+Bounded prototype design:
+
+- Add a guarded column-parallel rank-local trait/config:
+  `...colpar2halfo_pstage2_q200_p112_o56_qkscfix`.
+- Keep `C::CLUSTER_SIZE=2`, manual V movement, no VTMA/VSTMA, no multicast.
+- Treat the route as rank-local for TCGEN/TMA ownership, reusing the retained rowpar2 local wrappers.
+- Change tile scheduling only under the new guard:
+  - `tiles_per_cluster = NUM_SOFTMAXXERS`, not `NUM_SOFTMAXXERS * CLUSTER_SIZE`;
+  - both ranks use `q_tile_idx = t_coord.y`;
+  - `online_iters_for_row_cluster(t_coord.y)` uses row end `t_coord.y + 1`;
+  - output row validity uses `t_coord.y < tiles_m`.
+- Use `tt<float, Mb, Dvo/2>` for output TMEM under the new guard, keeping full-width output for all existing routes.
+- Preserve P handoff, P-scale TMEM, V-scale ping-pong, proxy/store-wait ordering, and qkscfix math.
+- Write each rank's normalized half-output directly to `g.o[{b, row, h, cta_rank * 64 + col}]`; rank 0 writes LSE.
+
+Risks:
+
+- Manual output store is slower than the existing full-tile TMA store, but it is the smallest correctness-first stitch/merge implementation without adding a new half-output global descriptor.
+- Both CTA ranks duplicate QK/softmax/P work for one row tile, so this is a structural resource probe, not expected to be faster unless PV feed gains outweigh duplicated producer work.
+- Any compile failure is likely to expose remaining full-width assumptions in direct-rescale/dual-output helpers.
