+Why local reset is unsafe:
+
+- Current semaphore init occurs once at `2126`-`2273`, then `__syncthreads(); fp4pv_cluster_sync<C>();` runs once before divergent role branches.
+- After that point, each role owns a separate `cur_bid` loop. There is no all-WG/all-CTA task-tail rendezvous.
+- Resetting semaphores in one role can race outstanding waits/arrives in another role from the previous task.
+- Resetting local phase masks alone is also unsafe because the underlying semaphore epoch remains carried.
+- Existing `normalize_p_stage_task_boundary(...)` is quant-side pstage3 bookkeeping only. It does not cover default pstage2, Q/K/V loader phases, V-scale TMEM, P-scale TMEM, PV issue, output, or output-store completion.
+
+Required persistent-long design:
+
+```cpp
+// One guarded route only: current 3WG cluster1 VTMA/VSTMA qkscfix pstage2.
+prefetch_tma_descriptors_once();
+allocate_shared_and_tmem_once();
+
+for (int cur_bid = blockIdx.x; cur_bid < total_bids; cur_bid += gridDim.x) {
+    int3 t_coord = get_tile_idx(cur_bid);
+    TaskMeta task = compute_task_meta(t_coord);
+    bool task_valid_for_rank = ...;  // no early continue may bypass barriers
+
+    if (threadIdx.x == 0) {
+        init_task_semaphores_exactly_as_startup();
+        init_task_shared_flags_and_descriptors();
+    }
+    __syncthreads();
+    fp4pv_cluster_sync<C>();
+
+    if (warpgroup::groupid() == PRODUCER_WG) {
+        run_producer_loader_task(task, task_valid_for_rank);
+        run_producer_scale_task_if_owner(task, task_valid_for_rank);
+        run_qk_pv_issue_task_if_owner(task, task_valid_for_rank);
+    } else if (warpgroup::groupid() == OUTPUT_WG) {
+        run_output_task(task, task_valid_for_rank);
+    } else if (warpgroup::groupid() == QUANT_WG0) {
+        run_quant_p_task(task, task_valid_for_rank);
+    }
+
+    task_tail_drain_for_role(task);
+    __syncthreads();
+    fp4pv_cluster_sync<C>();
+}
+```
+
+Task metadata that should be computed once per task:
+
+- `t_coord`, `q_iter_begin`, `iters_per_task`, `q_tiles_this_cluster`, `q_tile_idx`, `q_tile_rank_active`, `row_tile_valid`, `wait_remote_p_quant`, `wait_remote_tt_output`, `scale_log2`, `ZERO_SCALE`.
+- For external-LSE or inactive-row cases, use predicates and zero-iteration loops rather than `continue`, so all WGs still hit both task barriers.
+
+Task-tail drain requirements before reinitializing semaphores:
+
+- Producer loader:
+  - all outstanding Q/K/V loads for the task completed or their completion semaphores consumed by the downstream role;
+  - no `producer_v_sync_sem` phase outstanding.
+- V-scale helper:
+  - all V payload arrivals consumed;
+  - all V-scale TMEM stores issued and signaled;
+  - all `v_sc_tmem_reusable` arrivals for consumed slots observed before next task reset.
+- P-scale/P payload:
+  - all score-derived P payload stores have proxy visibility;
+  - all direct P-scale TMEM stores have `fp4pv_tmem_store_wait()` and `p_sc_tmem_ready` consumed;
+  - all `p_sc_tmem_reusable` and `p_stage_reusable` releases for consumed tiles observed.
+- QK/PV issue:
+  - all `scores_arrived` for issued QK consumed;
+  - all `p_copy_done` tails accounted;
+  - final PV issued and `tile_arrived` / `pv_final_ready` signaled.
+- Output:
+  - final `tile_arrived`/`pv_final_ready` consumed;
+  - final correction/rescale complete;
+  - global output/LSE store issued and `warpgroup::tma::store_async_wait<0>()` complete before task-tail barrier;
+  - output reuse semaphores emitted.
