+## 2026-06-15 - Legal split-correction K64 audit for qkscfix
+
+User directive: continue P bottleneck work after the cleaned rejected K64 half-start. Audit whether qid1/K64 half0 can be made legal by publishing a half0-safe correction/ready contract, or whether correction is inherently full-tile. No default/manual/bwd changes.
+
+Current live baseline:
+
+- Default/control route remains:
+  `dualaccum_directrescale_scorepack_prescaled_floor_x1sc_fusedmax_diagzero_prepub_earlyreuse_arrivereuse_pscreusefold_skippscarrive_vtma_vstma_pstage2_q200_p112_o56_qkscfix`.
+- Shape/path: 3WG, cluster1, `Mb=128`, `Nb=128`, `Dqk=192`, `Dvo=128`, VTMA/VSTMA, score-derived prescaled P payload, direct x1 P-scale TMEM, dual output accumulator direct-after-rescale, `P_STAGE_SLOTS=2`, `P_SCALE_TMEM_SLOTS=2`, `V_SCALE_TMEM_SLOTS=2`.
+- Existing `STATIC_ONLINE_MXFP4_SPLIT_P_READY_K64` does not apply to qkscfix score-derived P. It is currently limited to early fixed-scale FP32 pack or localmax split-quant routes.
+
+Protocol inventory:
+
+- PV side:
+  - `run_iteration()` waits `rescale_finished[0]` before non-first PV issue on the direct-after-rescale baseline.
+  - `wait_and_stage_p_sc()` waits `p_sc_tmem_ready[p_sc_slot]` before `issue_pv()`.
+  - `issue_pv()` only waits `p_online_k64_ready[p_buf][0/1]` inside the K64 split issue path, so P-scale readiness still gates half0.
+- Output side:
+  - `wait_corr_for_score(idx)` consumes `corr_arrived[0]` for each score tile in the non-early/non-pair baseline.
+  - For direct-after-rescale MXFP4 PV, output reads `corr_vec_smem[0]`, rescales old `tt_output` by that correction, then arrives `rescale_finished[0]`.
+  - Final LSE/normalization reads `max_vec_smem[0]` as row-sum and `lse_smem[0]` as row-max only after the full tile loop and the final stats phase.
+- Quant/producer side:
+  - qkscfix fused block-max computes all qid block maxima (`qid=0..3`) before payload conversion.
+  - Therefore full-tile `row_max` and MXFP4 output correction `acc_scale = exp2((row_max_old - row_max) * scale_log2)` are known before qid0/qid1 payload conversion.
+  - Score-derived P-scale words (`p_score_mx_packed_scales`) are also known before payload conversion.
+  - Full `row_sum = row_sum * acc_scale + tile_sum` is only known after all qids have generated exp2 values and tile-sum contributions.
+
+Legality conclusion:
+
+- Correction is not inherently full-tile for MXFP4 PV. The output-rescale correction needed before PV consumes any part of the current tile is `acc_scale`, and qkscfix fused block-max makes it available before half0 payload.
+- Row-sum/LSE is inherently full-tile, but PV does not need it for partial K64 consumption; it must remain on the existing final stats phase.
+- A bounded legal route is possible if and only if it:
+  - publishes `corr_vec_smem[0] = acc_scale`/`corr_arrived[0]` before half0;
+  - waits the previous `rescale_finished[0]` phase before overwriting the single correction slot;
+  - stages direct x1 P-scale TMEM and arrives `p_sc_tmem_ready[p_sc_slot]` before half0;
+  - publishes/arrives half0 only after qid0/qid1 payload stores and diagonal zeroing for groups 0..1;
+  - publishes/arrives half1 only after qid2/qid3 payload stores and diagonal zeroing for groups 2..3;
+  - suppresses the old late per-tile `corr_arrived` and `p_sc_tmem_ready` arrives for this guarded route;
+  - preserves full-tile `row_sum`, final stats publication, V-scale ping-pong, P/V scale reuse, mbarrier/proxy/store-wait ordering, and default/manual routes.
+
